 ## Overview
-Ray Evaluation Stepping DVR is a fixed-step ray marching technique for Direct Volume Rendering that integrates density and color along a ray, supporting configurable density ranges and early-out termination [S1, unofficial]. It determines the step size based on whether the volume supports object-space or world-space indexing, and uses a modular shader define system to swap transfer functions, blending, and BRDF evaluations at compile time [S1, unofficial].
+Ray Evaluation Stepping DVR is a fixed-step ray marching technique for Direct Volume Rendering that integrates density and color along a ray, supporting configurable density ranges and early-out termination [S1, unofficial]. It determines the step size based on whether the volume supports object-space or world-space indexing, and uses a modular shader define system to swap transfer functions, blending, and BRDF evaluations at compile time [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Fixed Step Ray Marching](3136-fixed-step-ray-marching.md) and differs from [Ray Marching Volume Rendering](1735-ray-marching-volume-rendering.md) by explicitly separating step-size configuration from the marching loop, and from [Density Marching](3462-density-marching.md) by supporting direct color output modes and warp-synchronized tracing checks [S1, unofficial].
 
